      "id": "APC-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "A progression count uniform in the possible exceptional zero",
      "anchor": "inputs-progression-count",
      "equations": [
        "inputs-progression-main",
        "inputs-progression-floor"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "PRE-02"
      ],
      "hypotheses": "Fix ε>0. Uniformly for sufficiently large Y, positive m divisible by 8, (a,m)=1, U>0 with (log Y)² log m/4≤log U and Y^(ε/6)≤log U≤Y^(ε/5)(log Y)². A quadratic exceptional pair is optional.",
      "statement": "There are at least U^(9/10) primes in (√U,U] congruent to a modulo m. The corrected main term B is at least cU/(2 log(U)m²) even when the residue sign maximizes the exceptional subtraction.",
      "definitions": [
        "π(U;m,a)",
        "li normalized to vanish at 2",
        "PNTAPRelW",
        "exceptional pair",
        "relative error",
        "candidate interval"
      ],
      "correspondence": "The progression error becomes at most half of the corrected main term. At the worst quadratic sign a Siegel bound at exponent one yields a gap U−U^β≥cU/(2m). The stage threshold pays for the denominator m² log U, then sieves away every integer through √U.",
